<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free State of Brunswick</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1946 CE · capital Brunswick</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Republican successor of the Duchy of Brunswick, remembered for giving Adolf Hitler German citizenship in 1932.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-augustus-duke-of-brunswick">Duke Ernest Augustus</a> abdicated on 8 November 1918, and a socialist republic was proclaimed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a>. After a period of councils and unrest, a constitution was adopted in 1922, making Brunswick a parliamentary free state.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a> had industry, canning and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bussing">Büssing</a> vehicle works, and its politics were polarised between Social Democrats and the right. From 1930 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazism">Nazis</a> shared government, and in February 1932 the Nazi interior minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dietrich-klagges">Dietrich Klagges</a> appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a> to a nominal post in the state's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> legation, which made the stateless Hitler a German citizen and allowed him to run for president.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After 1945 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a> was in the British zone. In November 1946 it was merged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-oldenburg">Oldenburg</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-schaumburg-lippe">Schaumburg-Lippe</a> into the new state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-saxony">Lower Saxony</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/free-state-of-brunswick.jpg" alt="Free State of Brunswick" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_Herzogtum_Braunschweig.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1946 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Brunswick</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Dietrich Klagges</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Freistaat Braunschweig</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1932&amp;focus=free-state-of-brunswick" aria-label="Free State of Brunswick on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4917 373 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Free State of Brunswick lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5237 629L5237 629M5237 629L5300 622M5237 629L5300 622"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5237 629h0M5300 622h0M5300 622h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5237 629h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5237 629h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Brunswick. <a href="/atlas?year=1932&amp;focus=free-state-of-brunswick">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
